.TH WSTUDIO 1 "2026-07-29" "wstudio 1.0.0-beta.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wstudio \- keyboard-centric digital audio workstation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wstudio
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B wstudio
.B \-\-tui
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B wstudio
.B \-\-gui
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B wstudio
.B render
.RI [ project.wsj
.RI [ output.wav ]]
.br
.B wstudio
.B clap\-scan
.br
.B wstudio
.B devices
.br
.B wstudio
.RB { \-v | \-\-version }
.br
.B wstudio
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wstudio
is a digital audio workstation for the terminal and as a native GUI.
It borrows vim's modal editing model instead of a mouse-first workflow:
.B normal
mode navigates the project and drives the transport,
.B insert
turns the keyboard into a piano,
.B visual
selects and yanks ranges, and
.B command
mode runs
.B :
commands. It ships with synths, samplers, a drum machine, a
sample-chopping slicer, a SoundFont player, and a full effects rack (gate,
compressor, multiband compressor, OTT, EQ, saturation, bitcrush, chorus,
phaser, flanger, tape, frequency shifter, delay, reverb) built in. It also
hosts external CLAP 1.2 instruments and effects.
.PP
With no arguments,
.B wstudio
launches on a blank project using the frontend selected by
.I wstudio.o.preferred_frontend
in the user's Lua configuration (default: the terminal frontend). Pass a
path to a
.I .wsj
project file to open it instead of starting blank.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.RI [ path ]
Open the given
.I .wsj
project file instead of starting on a blank project.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Force the terminal frontend for this run, overriding
.IR wstudio.o.preferred_frontend .
Errors if the terminal frontend was disabled at build time.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Force the native GUI frontend for this run, overriding
.IR wstudio.o.preferred_frontend .
Errors if the GUI frontend was disabled at build time.
.TP
.B render
Render a built-in demo melody through a synth, compressor, delay, and
reverb to
.I out.wav
in the current directory, then exit. Does not open a frontend; useful for
sanity-checking the audio pipeline.
With a project path, renders that saved session instead. Optional output path
defaults to
.IR bounce.wav .
.TP
.B clap\-scan
List every installed CLAP plugin as
.I <plugin-id> <name> <path>
and exit. Discovery follows
.I CLAP_PATH
and the platform paths the CLAP specification requires, or only
.I wstudio.o.clap_plugin_path
when that option is set.
.TP
.B vst3\-scan
List every installed VST3 audio-module class as
.I <class-id> <name> <path>
and exit. Discovery uses standard platform VST3 directories, or only
.I wstudio.o.vst3_plugin_path
when that option is set.
.TP
.B devices
List backend-native audio input, audio output, and live MIDI input device
identifiers for use with
.IR wstudio.o.audio_input_device ,
.IR wstudio.o.audio_output_device ,
and
.IR wstudio.o.midi_input_device ,
then exit.
.TP
.BI \-u " path"
Load
.I path
as the Lua configuration instead of the usual search
.RI ( $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wstudio/init.lua ", then " /etc/xdg/wstudio/init.lua ).
.B \-u NONE
skips loading any configuration file. May appear anywhere on the command
line.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B wstudio
is scripted with Lua: options, keymaps, custom
.B :
commands, and autocmds. On first run it writes a fully documented
template to the user configuration file below. A broken configuration is
reported but never blocks startup.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wstudio/init.lua
.RI ( ~/.config/wstudio/init.lua " when " XDG_CONFIG_HOME " is unset)
Per-user Lua configuration, generated on first run if missing.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/wstudio/init.lua
Optional system-wide Lua configuration, read before the user
configuration. On NixOS this is written by the
.I programs.wstudio
module.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wstudio/bookmarks.json
File-browser bookmarks. This store and the three below sit in the same
directory as
.IR init.lua .
They are optional conveniences: an unreadable or missing file leaves the
matching list empty and never blocks startup. A file left at the older
.I ~/.config/wstudio/
location by a previous release is still read, and moves here on the next
save.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wstudio/cmd_history.json
The last 50 submitted
.B :
commands.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wstudio/instrument_presets.wspreset
User-saved instrument presets, each with its ordered FX chain.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wstudio/drum_kits.json
User-saved drum pad tuning.
.TP
.I *.wsj
wstudio project files, passed as the optional
.I path
argument.
.TP
.I *.wsj~
The autosave backup written beside a project, loaded by
.BR :restore-backup .
.SH SEE ALSO
The Lua configuration API, the user-state storage conventions, and the file
format history ship with the source distribution under
.IR docs/lua-api.md ", " docs/user-config-storage.md ", and " FORMAT.md .
